                <pb facs="0477" n="419" sameAs="frus:frus1866p3/pg419"/>


                <head>Department of State, Office of War and Marine–Section first.</head>
                <p>By your despatch of the 8th instant, the President of the republic is pleased to
                    learn that you have occupied Nazas, held by 100 traitors, five of which you
                    killed, took 12 wounded and 59 prisoners, among them the two chiefs, badly
                    wounded.</p>
                <p>Independence and liberty! Chihuahua, August, 16, 1866.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>MEJIA.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>General <hi rendition="#small-caps">Francisco Arce</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">at Nazas</hi>.</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
